---
import { EXAMPLE_ANIMALS as animals, EXAMPLE_REPORT as result, EXAMPLE_SCOPE as scope } from '../data/sciground-example';
interface Props { full?: boolean }
const {full=false}=Astro.props;
const y=(value:number)=>260-(value-21)*40;
const groups=[{name:'Control',x:145,color:'#233d4c',summary:result.control},{name:'Treatment',x:320,color:'#a77b32',summary:result.treatment}];
const number=(value:number)=>value.toFixed(2).replace('-','−');
---
<article class="sg-report-sheet" aria-label="Illustrative report using synthetic data">
  <div class="sg-report-masthead"><span class="sg-report-brand">SciGround <span>/ Research report</span></span><span>Illustrative · Synthetic data</span></div>
  <div class="sg-report-heading"><div><p class="sg-kicker">Two-group comparison / Corrected input</p><h3>{scope.title}</h3></div><span class="sg-report-version">Example 001<br />Revision 02</span></div>
  <div class="sg-report-content"><figure class="sg-result-figure"><p class="sg-plot-title">Body weight (g)</p><svg viewBox="0 0 450 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="plot-title plot-desc"><title id="plot-title">Individual body weights in control and treatment groups</title><desc id="plot-desc">Ten synthetic animals per group. Control mean24.92g; treatment mean22.84g. Horizontal bars show group means. M17 is highlighted in Control at26.2g. Each dot is one animal.</desc>{[21,22,23,24,25,26,27].map(tick=><g><line x1="55" x2="420" y1={y(tick)} y2={y(tick)} class="sg-chart-grid"/><text x="41" y={y(tick)+4} text-anchor="end" class="sg-axis-tick">{tick}</text></g>)}{groups.map(group=><g>{animals.filter(a=>a.group===group.name).map((animal,index)=><circle cx={group.x+[-21,12,-8,25,-17,4,20,-2,-27,0][index]} cy={y(animal.weight)} r={animal.id==='M17'?6.5:5.2} fill={group.color} fill-opacity={animal.id==='M17'?1:.68}><title>{animal.id}: {animal.weight.toFixed(1)} g, {animal.group}</title></circle>)}<line x1={group.x-39} x2={group.x+39} y1={y(group.summary.mean)} y2={y(group.summary.mean)} stroke={group.color} stroke-width="2.5"/><text x={group.x} y="289" text-anchor="middle" class="sg-axis-label">{group.name}</text><text x={group.x} y="311" text-anchor="middle" class="sg-axis-tick">n = {group.summary.n}</text></g>)}<line x1="155" y1={y(26.2)} x2="185" y2={y(26.2)-13} stroke="#233d4c" stroke-width="1"/><text x="189" y={y(26.2)-12} class="sg-point-label">M17</text></svg><figcaption>Each dot is one animal. Lines show group means. <button type="button" class="sg-source-link" data-source-link aria-controls="sample-evidence" hidden>M17 source ↗</button></figcaption></figure><div class="sg-result-summary"><p class="sg-kicker">Treatment − Control</p><p class="sg-result-number">{number(result.meanDifference)}<span>g</span></p><p class="sg-result-ci">95% CI {number(result.confidenceInterval.low)} to {number(result.confidenceInterval.high)} g</p><p class="sg-result-conclusion">Mean body weight was lower in the treatment group in this illustrative dataset.</p><table class="sg-result-table"><caption class="visually-hidden">Group summaries</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">n</th><th scope="col">Mean (g)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{groups.map(group=><tr><th scope="row">{group.name}</th><td>{group.summary.n}</td><td>{number(group.summary.mean)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p class="sg-result-method">Two-sided Welch t-test · p = 0.00001584</p></div></div>
  <div class="sg-report-limits"><div><strong>Method & conditions</strong><p>One measurement per animal at day 14. Independent observations and approximately normal outcomes assumed. Welch inference is approximate.</p></div><div><strong>What this does not establish</strong><p>Measurement accuracy, independence, or a causal treatment effect. All 20 supplied animals are included; no exclusions.</p></div></div>
  <details id="sample-evidence" class="sg-evidence-detail" open={full}><summary><span class="sg-evidence-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Follow the evidence <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="sg-evidence-detail-body"><div><span class="sg-kicker">Input correspondence</span><h4 id="sample-source-row" tabindex="-1">M17 → Control → 26.2 g</h4><dl class="sg-source-row"><div><dt>Animal ID</dt><dd>M17</dd></div><div><dt>Source group</dt><dd>Control</dd></div><div><dt>Day 14 weight</dt><dd>26.2 g</dd></div></dl><p>The corrected group agrees with the supplied source row. The same value appears in the figure and contributes to the Control mean.</p><a href={scope.csvUrl} download>Download the synthetic source CSV ↗</a></div><div><span class="sg-kicker">Calculation basis</span><h4>20 observations. One comparison.</h4><p>Welch t = {number(result.t)}; df = {result.df.toFixed(3)}. The interval uses the same group direction as the reported difference. Values are rounded for display.</p><p class="sg-fine">Computed illustrative values, not an issued SciGround verification record.</p></div><div><span class="sg-kicker">Declared, not verified</span><h4>Research assumptions stay visible.</h4><p>Agreement with a supplied record does not prove true animal identity, accurate measurements, random assignment, or absence of cage effects.</p></div></div></details>
</article>

<script>
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-source-link]').forEach(button=>{
 button.hidden=false;
 button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
  const evidence=document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('#sample-evidence');
  if(evidence){evidence.open=true;document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#sample-source-row')?.focus();}
 });
});
</script>
